  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: Cli\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: Cli\n       Program: commons-cli\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Cli/Cli.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/commons-cli.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Cli/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 39\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: Cli-2\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\n2ff9573ffb08dd52ec3a55a49f2d77a1e94efbdf\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2007-05-22 17:47:16 +0000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\nCLI-51\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CLI-51\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.apache.commons.cli.bug.BugCLI51Test::test\n   --> org.apache.commons.cli.UnrecognizedOptionException: Unrecognized option: -o\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.apache.commons.cli.PosixParser\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: [cli] Parameter value \"-something\" misinterpreted as a parameter\nType: Bug | Priority: Critical | Status: Closed | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nIf a parameter value is passed that contains a hyphen as the (delimited) first \ncharacter, CLI parses this a parameter. For example using the call\njava myclass -t \"-something\"\nResults in the parser creating the invalid parameter -o (noting that it is \nskipping the 's')\n\nMy code is using the Posix parser as follows\nOptions options = buildCommandLineOptions();\nCommandLineParser parser = new PosixParser();\nCommandLine commandLine = null;\ntry {\n\t\t\t\n\tcommandLine = parser.parse(options, args);\n}\ncatch (ParseException e) {\n\t\t\t\n\tSystem.out.println(\"Invalid parameters. \" + e.getMessage() + NEW_LINE);\n\tSystem.exit(EXIT_CODE_ERROR);\n}\n\nThis has been tested against the nightly build dated 20050503.\n\nComments:\n\n[Henri Yandell]: The usual strategy here is to allow -- as a way to indicate that the rest of the\nline is pure text. If it's not available, this should be added.\n\n[Brian Egge]: Fix so parser doesn't burst options which are not defined. (-s) in the above case.  \n\nIncludes unit test.\n\n[Henri Yandell]: Thanks for the patch Brian; could you repeat it without the automatic IDE refactoring? It makes it a lot harder to read the patch; and more importantly for people to look back at the changes and see what the actual change was.\n\nChanging from protected to private for burstToken is also often a tricky one to do as we're stuck in the wonderful world of maintaining backwards compatibility.\n\nThe unit test looks good, but it'll need an Apache license and not an LGPL license (copy the header from the BugCLI18Test class).\n\n[Brian Egge]: Updated patch.  Removed incorrect license header; removed formatting changed; reverted access level change.\n\n[Brian Egge]: Has anyone had the chance to try out the updated patch for this issue?",
  "fix_diff": "--- org.apache.commons.cli.PosixParser (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.cli.PosixParser (fixed)\n@@ -302,8 +302,9 @@\n             }\n             else\n             {\n-                tokens.add(\"-\" + ch);\n-            }\n-        }\n-    }\n-}\n+                tokens.add(token);\n+                break;\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+}"
}